As $Z \ge a$ implies $\paren {Z + u}^2 \ge \paren {a + u}^2$, [[Markov's Inequality]] gives:
{{begin-eqn}}
{{eqn | l = \map \Pr {Z \ge a}
| o = \le
| r = \frac {\expect {\paren {Z + u}^2} } {\paren {a + u}^2}
| c = [[Markov's Inequality]]
}}
{{eqn | r = \frac {\sigma^2 + u^2} {\paren {a + u}^2}
| c = as $\expect Z = 0$
}}
{{end-eqn}}
